  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1236 PM MDT Sat Oct 17 2026\n\nUpper-level ridging remains firmly established across eastern \nIdaho today, supporting pleasant autumn conditions and above-\nnormal temperatures through the remainder of the weekend and \nstarting off the work week. Highs will remain in the mid-to-\nupper 60s to lower 70s across the Snake River Plain and Eastern \nMagic Valley, with light afternoon winds. Meanwhile, an \nexpansive upper-level low is currently digging south along the \nPacific Northwest coastline.\n\nAs the low drops south off the California coast early next \nweek, southerly flow aloft will gradually tap into Pacific \nmoisture. Deterministic guidance points toward isolated light \nshower activity returning as early as Tuesday into Wednesday \nacross south-central and eastern Idaho. A more organized, \nwidespread round of precipitation continues to be favored late \nThursday through Friday as the upper trough lifts northeast into\nNevada and the Great Basin. While ensemble clusters show subtle\ntiming and positional differences regarding the main trough \naxis, cooler temperatures and increased PoPs remain on track \nheading into late week.",
